{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And Leah conceived and bore a son.</b> In every case Scripture mentions ותהר ותלד to indicate the immediacy of the event. And it attached birth to pregnancy because each of them gave birth at seven months, since during the seven years, the second period of Rachel's labor, all the tribes were born, all of them, apart from Binyamin. And I shall mention for you the reason for those born at seven months, that they live, while those born at eight months die. Know that each and every one of the seven planets serves for one month, and their order is likewise שצ״ם חנכ״ל. But the order of Creation is חל״ם כצנ״ש for the seven days of Creation. And this order of the months of pregnancy: Shabbetai serves the first month, and Tzedek the second, and so for all of them until Levanah, which is the seventh, and it is the star appointed over life. Therefore one born in the seventh month will live. But when it enters Shabbetai, which returns cyclically and is the eighth — for the nature of Shabbetai is cold and dry, which is the nature of death — therefore the infant is not alive in the eighth month, for it will kill it by its nature, which is the nature of death, and will return it to a drop as it was at first. But when it passes the eighth it enters the ninth, which is Tzedek, and it is the star of life and of good — then it will live. And behold, most of those born are born at nine months, and they are under the star Tzedek, which is the ninth in the cyclical return; and some are born at ten months, and they are under Ma'adim; and some are born at eleven months, and they are under Chamah. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: a case occurred with Rabbah Tosfa'ah whose wife's pregnancy lasted twelve months of the year, and he declared it valid — that is, even though her husband was not continually present with her, nevertheless he declared it valid and did not classify it as a mamzer but as valid, for as long as twelve months have not yet passed we say: the majority of acts of intercourse follow the husband, for sometimes the infant delays twelve months." "<b>And know</b> that of these seven planets, two of them are very good and beneficial, and they are Tzedek and Nogah. And two of them are very harmful, and they are Shabbetai and Ma'adim. And two of them are luminous, and they are Chamah and Levanah; and there remains one star that is intermediate, pairing good with the good and evil with the evil ones." "<b>And she called his name Reuven.</b> The naming of the tribes by our mothers Leah and Rachel was all through ruach ha-kodesh, according to the attributes of the Holy One, blessed be He. For Leah, in her four sons, alluded to all ten from below upward. She called the first Reuven, corresponding to the attribute of Judgment — it is the final ה in the Name — for from it comes to her the power of generation. And she knew this from Avraham, in whose name the letter ה was added, and so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: אברם does not beget, אברהם begets. And the word ראובן is from the root of ראייה, seeing, for seeing is through the power of the ה, which is the attribute of Judgment, and for this reason the evil eye has great power. And similarly Shim'on is from the root of שמיעה, hearing, for hearing is through the power of the ו״ו in the Name, which is the ו׳ of the extremities; and therefore she said: כי ראה ה׳ כי שנואה אנכי — for HaShem has seen that I am hated — and afterward וישמע ה׳ אל קולי — and HaShem has heard my voice. Here you have Reuven and Shim'on corresponding to the attribute of Judgment and its six extremities included within it; and so was their intention with all the rest of the tribes in their names. I shall explain each one of them in its place; incline your ear to their explanation."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:32.803556497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}